   "e": 11.03,
   "dur": 11.03,
   "dicho": "This editing style is taking over in 2026 and every single editor wants to learn it. So here's a quick breakdown of how it's made. There's really three steps to making this editing style. First is the background."
  },
  {
   "id": 2,
   "s": 11.03,
   "e": 18.07,
   "dur": 7.03,
   "dicho": "The background is typically white, layered on with a grid effect. It also has a half -told texture and even a casted shadow."
  },
  {
   "id": 3,
   "s": 18.07,
   "e": 24.13,
   "dur": 6.07,
   "dicho": "The second step is your main object. There are two types of scenes in this editing style. Object centric and text centric."
  },
  {
   "id": 4,
   "s": 24.13,
   "e": 30.3,
   "dur": 6.17,
   "dicho": "Just take your main object and place it in the middle. Then stylize it with desaturation, a texture and a casted shadow. The"
  },
  {
   "id": 5,
   "s": 30.3,
   "e": 32.57,
   "dur": 2.27,
   "dicho": "third step is your complementary object."
  },
  {
   "id": 6,
   "s": 32.57,
   "e": 36.47,
   "dur": 3.9,
   "dicho": "This is the text that comes behind or around your object to help visualize it."
  },
  {
   "id": 7,
   "s": 36.47,
   "e": 38.53,
   "dur": 2.07,
   "dicho": "And finally, it's your depth elements."
  },
  {
   "id": 8,
   "s": 38.53,
   "e": 43.27,
   "dur": 4.73,
   "dicho": "These are the elements on the edges of the screen with a blur and a darken effect to give you some depth."
  },
  {
   "id": 9,
   "s": 43.27,
   "e": 50.33,
   "dur": 7.07,
   "dicho": "If you would like to watch me create this scene over here step by step, I've made a full tutorial breaking it down on YouTube. Just go ahead and check it out."
  }
